+    and T any assigned tool with a comparing branch, and let s be any statement
+    T confirms. Then F' = s + ", therefore " + F proposes exactly what F
+    proposes and satisfies `fix_computing != 0`. So for EVERY F there is a
+    semantically equivalent F' that passes the fix-side conjunct: the conjunct
+    `bool(fix_computing)` alone restricts nothing. A gate satisfiable by
+    prepending a constant to any input is not a gate. Demonstrated by execution
