C (adopted) 5 of 5 and 7 of 7.** C dominates both. For C's P2, 7 of 7, Wilson 95% is [0.645670, 1.000000] and Clopper-Pearson [0.590384, 1.000000], every interval cross-checked on 2 independent routes with a maximum gap of 2.776e-16. **AND `astronomical`'s RECORDED REASON WAS ALSO WRONG.** It is NOT truth-blind: it CONFIRMS the true SI speed of light and REJECTS 3000000 m/s, so it discriminates coarsely. It confirms `299792459 m/s`, false by 1 m/s, because its tolerance is 1% — so it is a TOLERANT COMPARATOR that can solely admit a false exact-value claim, which is the real reason it may not admit alone. My earlier reading came from a probe pair whose BOTH members were in km/s, where its separate unit defect rejects everything: the pair shared the feature that caused the result. **3 STRUCTURAL GUARDS NOW MAKE THE ERROR CLASS UNREPEATABLE**, because the same error occurred 3 times in one night from 3 different authors: the producer ENUMERATES each verifier's favourable branches by bounding the function with the SYNTAX TREE and EXITS NON-ZERO if its probe set covers fewer branches than exist; it DERIVES both tables from its own rows; and it IMPORTS the live tables and exits non-zero on any drift between what ships and what the measurement justifies. A character-window scan was tried first and leaked across the function boundary, attributing one verifier's branches to its neighbour. Guard: `bench/tests/test_a_confirming_tool_must_discriminate_to_admit_2026-11-10.py`, 17 tests, 3 of 3 mutations red in BOTH the guard and the producer.
