E, returns UNCERTAIN rather than REJECTED, so it fails in that direction too. **IT ALSO CONTAMINATES AN AGREEMENT, WHICH IS WHY THE CONTROL MATTERED.** On the corpus, SM-08 is a FALSE claim this tool REJECTED and that was counted as agreement. But it rejects mixed-dimension claims whatever their truth, so the agreement reflects how often such claims happen to be false rather than any judgement the tool made. Of the 3 agreements in that measurement only 2 are discriminating — `statsmodels` on ST-01 and `stoichiometric_balance` on CM-10, both CONFIRMED. **THE BLAST RADIUS IS THE K/L/M CELLS.** `dimensional_analysis` sits in the PRIMARY tool list for **physics, chemistry, engineering and cross_domain**. Physics, chemistry and engineering are the K, L and M specialist cells promoted from shadow to LIVE on 2026-07-27 on his own standing instruction, superseding constraint S5 of the Exp 40 plan, whose condition was that they *stay in shadow until their tool coverage is validated*. **That validation was never performed**: 0 files under `scripts/` or `bench/tests/` match `specialist.*accuracy` or `accuracy.*specialist`; `test_shadow_audit_klm.py` pins the audit RECORD'S SCHEMA, which its own docstring calls the instrument built to SUPPORT the check; and `test_specialist_live_promotion.py` asserts MEMBERSHIP in `LIVE_SPECIALIST_DOMAINS` while still quoting S5's unmet condition. **AND PHYSICS HAS 0 DOCUMENTS IN THE CORPUS**, so it is live with no content of ours to measure it on at all. **WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT COST TODAY.** It does NOT change an apply-back decision: a prose target was refused before the 2026-11-10 domain route existed, so a false rejection yields the status quo. It DOES write a FALSE REASON, which is the precise harm B88's original defect caused 34 times, and the refusal detail was narrowed the same night so the tool verdict is appended as advisory rather than given as the ground. **AND IT MATTERS FOR BENCH RUN 2 RATHER THAN FOR TONIGHT:** a live specialist that rejects correct physics is a false-positive source in exactly the domains BR2 is meant to cover. **NO FIX IS PROPOSED, DELIBERATELY.** A correct check needs the expression's STRUCTURE — which quantities are summed and which multiplied — and `pint` can supply that given a parsed expression rather than a bag of extracted quantities. That is a build on a live specialist tool in the primary pool of 4 domains, so under `p-pass-high-consequence-check` it is his to authorise rather than mine to take from a measurement. **[NEEDS HIS RULING] on whether to repair the predicate before Bench Run 2, or to move `dimensional_analysis` to `secondary_only` in the manifest so it can corroborate but never refuse, which is the smaller change and removes no capability.** Producers: `scripts/the_dimensional_check_tests_homogeneity_not_correctness_2026-11-10.py`, which exits 1 rather than 0 once the predicate is repaired so it cannot outlive its own defect; and `scripts/the_topics_tools_on_the_projects_own_corpus_2026-11-10.py` for the corpus measurement it came from. ★★★ **THE FALSE-ADMIT HALF IS NOW BUILT, AND THE ROUTE ADOPTED IS NOT THE ONE EITHER I OR THE PANEL FIRST PROPOSED, 2026-11-10.** Producer: `scripts/which_admissions_are_truth_blind_2026-11-10.py`. **THE CONTROL: a verdict that takes the same value on a claim and on a FALSE VARIANT of that claim carries 0 bits about the claim**, so admitting a fix on it is admission by vocabulary and not by tool. **MY FIRST NARROWING WAS REFUTED BY A FREE PANEL SEAT AND THE REFUTATION REPRODUCES.** I had excluded 2 tools, having measured `biological_sequence` as DISCRIMINATING. It has 5 favourable branches: 4 compare a computed value against the claim and 1 reports only that a sequence parses. My probe hit a comparing branch and generalised from it. Executed here: `the sequence 'ATGC' proves the defendant was present` and `the sequence 'ATGC' proves the moon is made of cheese` both return CONFIRMED at 0.85 with identical evidence. **THE SEAT'S OWN FIX WAS THEN MEASURED AND REFUSED.** It proposed excluding the tool outright. Scored on 2 named properties — truth-blind paths BARRED, and discriminating paths RETAINED — the tool-level exclusion gives 2 of 3 and 1 of 2, while gating that tool at its BRANCH gives 3 of 3 and 2 of 2. The exclusion removes a capability that demonstrably works, so under `additive-standard`'s removal clause it is refused. **AND THERE IS NO COMPOSABILITY CLAIM**: gating at the branch alone beats excluding the tool alone, so under his definition the SINGLE fix is preferred and composing the 2 would be composition for its own sake. **THE SAME MEASUREMENT FOUND A 3RD TRUTH-BLIND TOOL THE SEAT HAD JUDGED SAFE.** `chemistry_structure` CONFIRMS `the molecule CCO is ethanol` AND `the molecule CCO is benzene`, because it validates the SMILES string and not the claim; the seat recorded that its own probes never drew a CONFIRMED from it and that it was therefore rightly not excluded. **BUILT:** `CANNOT_ADMIT_ALONE` holds `dimensional_analysis`, `chemistry_structure` and `astronomical`; `BRANCH_GATED_ADMISSION` holds `biological_sequence` against the marker `matches claim`, which is READ OFF that verifier's own source and is TOOL-SCOPED. **APPLYING THAT MARKER GLOBALLY WAS MY OWN ERROR AND IT COST A POINT**: it barred `stoichiometric_balance`, which the same run measures as discriminating. **`definitive_for` IS UNCHANGED, so no favourable verdict is discarded and a corroborating voice is still recorded; only the ADMISSION narrows**, and the refusal detail now carries `for_but_cannot_admit=` so the record can tell *nothing agreed* from *only blind tools agreed*. **GUARD:** `bench/tests/test_a_confirming_tool_must_discriminate_to_admit_2026-11-10.py`, 13 tests, 4 of 4 mutations red. **ITS FIRST VERSION MISSED THE CORE DEFECT AND THAT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN QUIETLY FIXED**: reverting the admit line to the original `bool(definitive_for)` left all 12 of its tests GREEN, because every end-to-end probe it used was refused by a REJECTION from another tool, so the verdict never depended on the gate. The discriminating case is `the molecule CCO is benzene` in chemistry — FALSE, confirmed only by a truth-blind tool, with nothing speaking against it — and the guard now asserts that premise so it cannot rot into a probe that passes for the wrong reason. ★★★ **AND THE FIX I ADOPTED WAS ITSELF WRONG, FOUND BY A FREE PANEL SEAT AND REPRODUCED: IT DESTROYED A LIVE ADMISSION. Corrected 2026-11-10.** I had put `chemistry_structure` in `CANNOT_ADMIT_ALONE` at the TOOL level on a probe that drew only its SMILES-validity fallback. **The tool has 3 favourable branches and 2 of them COMPARE**: `the molecule 'CCO' has formula C2H6O` -> CONFIRMED with `matches claim`, the `C3H8O` variant -> REJECTED; same shape for molecular weight at 46.07 against 99.9 g/mol. **THE LOSS WAS LIVE, NOT LATENT**: that claim routes to `chemistry/mathematical`, the tool IS dispatched, and the tool-level bar returned `admits=False, for=-, for_but_cannot_admit=chemistry_structure` on a true, reachable, discriminating admission. **SO I COMMITTED THE EXACT 1-BRANCH-OF-N ERROR I HAD JUST REFUSED THE SEAT FOR, within the same hour**, and my measurement reported dominance because the probe set enumerated 1 of 3 branches. **THE CORRECTED CONFIGURATION IS DERIVED BY A RULE, NOT BY A LIST OF NAMES.** Gating at the BRANCH means letting a tool admit only where its own evidence shows it compared a computed value against the claim. A tool is gated that way where it has both a truth-blind and a comparing favourable branch, at the TOOL where every favourable branch is truth-blind, and not at all where none is. That yields `CANNOT_ADMIT_ALONE = {dimensional_analysis, astronomical}` and `BRANCH_GATED_ADMISSION = {biological_sequence, chemistry_structure}`. **RE-SCORED OVER FULLY ENUMERATED BRANCHES — 12 admitting paths, not 5 — the 3 options are A 4 of 5 and 3 of 7, B (what I committed) 5 of 5 and 5 of 7, C (adopted) 5 of 5 and 7 of 7.** C dominates both. For C's P2, 7 of 7, Wilson 95% is [0.645670, 1.000000] and Clopper-Pearson [0.590384, 1.000000], every interval cross-checked on 2 independent routes with a maximum gap of 2.776e-16. **AND `astronomical`'s RECORDED REASON WAS ALSO WRONG.** It is NOT truth-blind: it CONFIRMS the true SI speed of light and REJECTS 3000000 m/s, so it discriminates coarsely. It confirms `299792459 m/s`, false by 1 m/s, because its tolerance is 1% — so it is a TOLERANT COMPARATOR that can solely admit a false exact-value claim, which is the real reason it may not admit alone. My earlier reading came from a probe pair whose BOTH members were in km/s, where its separate unit defect rejects everything: the pair shared the feature that caused the result. **3 STRUCTURAL GUARDS NOW MAKE THE ERROR CLASS UNREPEATABLE**, because the same error occurred 3 times in one night from 3 different authors: the producer ENUMERATES each verifier's favourable branches by bounding the function with the SYNTAX TREE and EXITS NON-ZERO if its probe set covers fewer branches than exist; it DERIVES both tables from its own rows; and it IMPORTS the live tables and exits non-zero on any drift between what ships and what the measurement justifies. A character-window scan was tried first and leaked across the function boundary, attributing one verifier's branches to its neighbour. Guard: `bench/tests/test_a_confirming_tool_must_discriminate_to_admit_2026-11-10.py`, 17 tests, 3 of 3 mutations red in BOTH the guard and the producer.
