 **B137. `cross_domain` DECLARES 11 VERIFICATION TOOLS ACROSS 3 CLAIM TYPES AND HAS 0 CLAIM PATTERNS, SO EVERY ONE OF THEM IS UNREACHABLE BY CONSTRUCTION — AND `biology`'s PATTERNS CONTAIN 0 SEQUENCE WORDS.** Added 2026-11-10T06:05:00+00:00. **STATUS: PROPOSED, measured, root-caused, NOT FIXED. No ruling is requested yet; it is the same defect class B22 already records and belongs with that entry's repair.** **FOUND WHILE CHECKING WHETHER A GATE BUILT THE SAME NIGHT WAS REACHABLE**, which is the `additive-standard` symmetric question asked of my own work rather than of someone else's. Producer: `scripts/which_admissions_are_truth_blind_2026-11-10.py`, section 5. **THE MECHANISM.** `domain_classify_claim` returns `uncategorised` when a domain config carries no claim patterns, and `domain_b_cell_tools` then returns no tools for that claim type. **`cross_domain` has 0 compiled claim patterns against 3 claim types that each carry tools**, so all 11 distinct tools named there — `biological_sequence`, `chemistry_structure`, `dimensional_analysis`, `graph_property`, `ml_claim`, `scipy`, `statsmodels`, `sympy`, `uncertainty_propagation`, `wolfram` and `z3` — can never be dispatched in that domain. 1 of the 10 loaded domains is in this state, Wilson 95% [0.017876, 0.404150], Clopper-Pearson [0.002529, 0.445016]. **`biology` IS A DIFFERENT AND SUBTLER CASE and my first inference about it was wrong.** It is NOT pattern-less: it has 3 patterns for its 3 claim types. But **0 of them contain any of `sequence`, `dna`, `rna`, `protein`, `nucleotide`, `complement`, `codon` or `gc content`** — its `mathematical` pattern matches operators and enzyme-kinetics terms such as Km, Vmax and IC50 — so a sequence claim matches nothing. **MEASURED: 0 of 10 sequence claims reach `biological_sequence` across the 2 domain and claim-type pairs that assign it, Wilson 95% [0.000000, 0.277533], Clopper-Pearson [0.000000, 0.308497].** **THIS IS B22's `graph_property` FINDING GENERALISED**: a tool decl